      by Apple, and published on <a href={`${repo}/releases`}>GitHub Releases</a
      >. Clicker's built-in updater only installs updates signed with Clicker's
      own update key. Copies from anywhere else, or builds you compile yourself,
      aren't official releases, and Clicker can't vouch for them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clicker checks for updates as described in the <a href="/privacy"
        >Privacy Policy</a
      >. It's free, so updates come when they come: Clicker doesn't promise any
      particular fixes, features, support or release schedule, and development
      may stop at any time.
    </p>

